From f9a29dea33709de7f363f3ceb3c6f42424dfa114 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: unex <7575866+unex@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:58:38 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] backend/drm: allow a gamma LUT reset on a CRTC without gamma

Some drivers do not support a gamma LUT on the CRTC. For example,
meson has no GAMMA_LUT property and a legacy gamma size of 0.

On such a CRTC, drm_legacy_crtc_set_gamma() returns false for a
NULL LUT (a reset to the default LUT), and it logs nothing. There is
no LUT to reset, so the request is already satisfied.

The scene output sets gamma_lut_changed when the output is disabled.
The next build of the output state then adds a NULL color transform
to the state. wlr_output_test_state() drops this field, because it
does not change the output state, and the test passes. But
wlr_backend_commit() keeps all fields, and the DRM backend calls
drm_legacy_crtc_set_gamma(). The commit fails before the atomic
ioctl, with no log line.

On sway, the first "output * power on" after "output * power off"
fails with "Backend commit failed", and the output stays off. The
second request works, because gamma_lut_changed is false by then.

Return true when the CRTC has no gamma LUT and the caller requests a
reset.
---
 backend/drm/legacy.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/backend/drm/legacy.c b/backend/drm/legacy.c
index 223852e..48ec9ee 100644
--- a/backend/drm/legacy.c
+++ b/backend/drm/legacy.c
@@ -255,7 +255,8 @@ bool drm_legacy_crtc_set_gamma(struct wlr_drm_backend *drm,
 		// The legacy interface doesn't offer a way to reset the gamma LUT
 		size = drm_crtc_get_gamma_lut_size(drm, crtc);
 		if (size == 0) {
-			return false;
+			// The CRTC has no gamma LUT, so there is nothing to reset
+			return true;
 		}
 
 		linear_lut = malloc(3 * size * sizeof(uint16_t));
-- 
2.55.0

